SUMMARY
Tax manager with nine years in public accounting firms serving closely held businesses. I manage a book of about 180 clients covering federal and multi-state corporate returns, partnership and S-corp returns, and sales and use tax compliance, and I review everything that goes out the door for my team. Available on two to three weeks' notice.

EXPERIENCE
Pacific Crest Tax and Advisory, Tax Manager, San Diego, CA, Dec 2021 - Present
- Manage a team of 5 preparing and reviewing roughly 110 partnership (Form 1065) and S-corporation (Form 1120-S) returns and 45 C-corporation returns a year, including K-1 packages for about 500 partners and shareholders.
- Review federal and multi-state corporate returns for clients filing in up to 15 states, with apportionment, state modifications and pass-through entity tax elections modeled in Excel.
- Run the sales and use tax practice: monthly and quarterly filings for 30 clients across California, Arizona, Nevada and Texas, nexus reviews after online expansion, and two CDTFA audits closed with combined assessments reduced by 60%.
- Cut the review cycle from 6 days to 3 by standardizing the Excel workpaper binder and the reviewer checklist.
- Handle IRS and FTB correspondence for the client base and train seniors on notice responses.

Torrey Ledger CPAs, Tax Senior, San Diego, CA, Jul 2019 - Nov 2021
- Prepared and first-reviewed S-corp, partnership and corporate returns for restaurants, contractors and medical practices; built basis and at-risk schedules for partners.
- Prepared multi-state corporate returns for a distribution client with filings in 11 states.
- Set up sales tax compliance for new e-commerce clients, including marketplace facilitator rules.

Harbor Point Accounting, Tax Associate, San Diego, CA, Oct 2017 - Jun 2019
- Prepared individual, partnership and corporate returns and quarterly sales and use tax returns under senior review.

EDUCATION
B.S. Accounting, State University

